219: We resolve the minimality conjecture \cite[Conjecture~4.10]{RWY} about the basic ideals $J_v$:
220: \begin{theorem}\label{thm:main}
221: Given a bigrassmannian permutation $v=v_{r,s,t,n}\in S_n$ let
222: \begin{align*}
223: i&\coloneqq s-t+1,\\
224: j&\coloneqq r-t+1,\\
225: a&\coloneqq \min(n-r-i,r-j),\\
226: b&\coloneqq \min(i,j).
227: \end{align*}
228: Then the basic ideal $J_v$, thought of as an ideal of $H^*(\mathrm{Gr}_{r,n})\cong \Lambda/I_{r,n-r}$, is minimally generated by
229: \begin{equation}
230: \label{eqn:minimallist}
231: \{\overline{s}_{\mu} \mid i^j\subseteq \mu \subseteq (i^j,b^a)\}.
232: \end{equation}
233: \end{theorem}
234: That (\ref{eqn:minimallist}) generates $J_v$ is \cite[Theorem 4.8]{RWY}. The conjectural part, which we prove,
235: is the minimality claim, that is, no generator can be removed without changing the ideal.

702: \begin{lemma}
703: \label{lem:hopf-identity}
704: For any partitions $\lambda,\mu$ and any partition $\nu\neq \emptyset$,
705: \[\sum_{\lambda,\mu}(-1)^{|\lambda|}c_{\lambda,\mu}^{\nu}s_{\lambda'}s_{\mu}=0.\]
706: \end{lemma}
707: \begin{proof}
708: Recall the Hopf algebra structure on $\Lambda$ over $\mathbb{Z}$. This includes
709: \begin{itemize}
710: \item the usual multiplication map $\nabla:\Lambda\otimes \Lambda\to \Lambda$ with
711: \[\nabla(s_{\lambda}\otimes s_{\mu}) = s_{\lambda}s_{\mu};\]
712: \item the coproduct described previously, with $\Delta:\Lambda\to\Lambda\otimes\Lambda$ with
713: \[\Delta(s_\nu) = \sum_{\lambda,\mu}c_{\lambda,\mu}^{\nu}s_{\lambda}\otimes s_{\nu}; \]
714: \item the unit $\eta:\mathbb{Z}\to \Lambda$, the ring homomorphism with $1\mapsto 1$;
715: \item the counit $\epsilon:\Lambda\to\mathbb{Z}$ taking $f\in \lambda$ to its constant term $f(0,0,\ldots)$;
716: \item the antipode $S:\Lambda\to\Lambda$ with
717: \[S(s_{\lambda})=(-1)^{|\lambda|}s_{\lambda'}.\]
718: \end{itemize}
719: The antipode $S$ is characterized by the commutative diagram shown in Figure \ref{fig:diag}.
720: \begin{figure}[ht]
721: \[
722: \begin{tikzcd}[row sep=3.6em,column sep=1em]
723: & \Lambda\otimes \Lambda \arrow[rr,"S\otimes\mathrm{id}"] && \Lambda\otimes \Lambda \arrow[dr,"\nabla"] \\
724: \Lambda \arrow[ur,"\Delta"] \arrow[rr,"\varepsilon"] \arrow[dr,"\Delta"'] && \mathbb{Z} \arrow[rr,"\eta"] && \Lambda \\
725: & \Lambda\otimes \Lambda \arrow[rr,"\mathrm{id}\otimes S"'] && \Lambda\otimes \Lambda \arrow[ur,"\nabla"']
726: \end{tikzcd}
727: \]
728: \caption{The Hopf algebra stucture on $\Lambda$}
729: \label{fig:diag}
730: \end{figure}
731: On a Schur function $s_{\nu}$, we compute
732: \begin{align*}
733: \eta\circ\epsilon(s_{\nu}) &= \eta(0) = 0,\quad\mbox{and}\\
734: \nabla\circ(S\otimes \mathrm{id})\circ\Delta(s_{\nu})&=\nabla\left( \sum_{\lambda,\mu}c_{\lambda,\mu}^{\nu}S(s_{\lambda})\otimes s_{\nu}\right) = \sum_{\lambda,\mu}c_{\lambda,\mu}^{\nu} (-1)^{|\lambda|}s_{\lambda'}s_\mu. \qedhere
735: \end{align*}

833: \begin{remark}
834: In \cite{RWY}, a transposed version of Theorem \ref{thm:main} is also proved (with minimality conjectured). The generating set is
835: \begin{equation}
836: \label{eqn:transposedlist}
837: \{\overline{s}_{\mu} \mid i^j\subseteq \mu \subseteq ((i+a)^b,i^{j-b})\}.
838: \end{equation}
839: These are exactly the conjugates of the generating set (\ref{eqn:minimallist}) whose minimality we prove. One could straightforwardly``transpose'' all arguments in this paper to prove minimality of (\ref{eqn:transposedlist}). Specifically, one would interchange the roles of wide and
840: tall equations in Section~\ref{sec:theequations} (with minor modifications) and swap the order of the tensor components in Sections~\ref{sec:Hopf} and \ref{sec:conclusion}.
